      "writtenOn": "2025-07-17T05:45:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "+1,\n\nthanks for bringing this point.\n\nAll products based on the WCL utilize ISH5.8, allowing for some shared code across projects. However, hardware-specific mappings can vary depending on the project like below.\n\n\u003e I2C lines and sensor interrupt GPIOs between ISH and the sensors.\n\u003e EC-PCH GPIO interrupt mapping for DSP communication.\n\u003e Each platform may select different sensors based on board design.\n\u003e ISH UART port mapping (Intel recommending the use of ISH_UART0 by default)\n\nGiven these variations, certain files can be common across projects?\n\nzephyr/program/ocelot/ocelot-ish/interrupts.dtsi\nzephyr/program/ocelot/ocelot-ish/ish.dtsi\nzephyr/program/ocelot/ocelot-ish/prj.conf\n\nBoard-specific changes, such as ISH GPIOs and I2C sensor mappings, may differ between projects.\nThese can be managed using project-specific overlays OR separate fines?\nzephyr/program/ocelot/ocelot-ish/i2c.dtsi\nzephyr/program/ocelot/ocelot-ish/gpio.dtsi\nzephyr/program/ocelot/ocelot-ish/motionsense.dtsi\n\nAdditionally \u0027motionsense.dtsi\u0027 can be maintained as one copy for both EC,ISH sensing.\n\nLet us know your feedback.",
